id: pm-graph-g2fs
title: Drop inert pm manifest key and guard the closed manifest vocabulary
description: "pm-cli 2026.8.19 made its extension-manifest vocabulary a closed set of 18 keys; the inert top-level pm compatibility blob now produces manifest_unknown_key warnings (observed as strict-assertion CI failures in unbraind/pm-linear PRs #75/#76). Remove the key from manifest.json, pin @unbrained/pm-cli to 2026.8.22, add unbounded output-budget args to the changelog scripts so pm-changelog keeps reading the full workspace through the newer pinned CLI, and add a regression test asserting checkExtensionManifestCompatibility reports zero manifest_unknown_key findings."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-22T17:36:06.141Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-22T17:39:32.304Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-22T17:36:24.104Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-22T17:36:24.104Z"
author: ox-alpha
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-22T17:36:12.634Z",ox-alpha,"Verified with a temporary re-add of the pm key: test/manifest-vocabulary.test.ts fails (1 fail) while the key is present and passes once removed. npm test: 222 pass, 0 fail. release:check exit 0. ./node_modules/.bin/pm health --strict-exit exit 0 on the pinned 2026.8.22 binary."
